1)Launching an AWS EC2 Ubuntu Instance and Connecting Through Ubuntu Linux Terminal
Step-by-Step Procedure
Step 1: Create AWS Account
1.	Open AWS official website: 
AWS Official Website
2.	Click on: 
Create an AWS Account
3.	Enter: 
•	Email address 
•	Password 
•	AWS account name 
4.	Add payment details and complete verification. 
5.	Choose: 
Free Tier
________________________________________
Step 2: Open EC2 Dashboard
1.	Login to AWS Console. 
2.	Search: 
EC2
3.	Open: 
EC2 Dashboard
________________________________________
Step 3: Launch EC2 Instance
1.	Click: 
Launch Instance
2.	Enter instance name: 
MyUbuntuServer
________________________________________
Step 4: Choose Ubuntu AMI
Select:
Ubuntu Server 24.04 LTS
(Free Tier Eligible)
________________________________________
Step 5: Choose Instance Type
Select:
t2.micro
OR
t3.micro
These are free-tier eligible instance types.
________________________________________
Step 6: Create Key Pair
1.	Click: 
Create New Key Pair
2.	Enter key name: 
firstkey
3.	Select: 
RSA
4.	Select format: 
.pem
5.	Download the key file. 
Example:
firstkey.pem
________________________________________
Step 7: Configure Security Group
Allow:
SSH Traffic (Port 22)
Source:
Anywhere
This allows terminal connection.
________________________________________
Step 8: Launch Instance
Click:
Launch Instance
Wait for instance to start.
________________________________________
Step 9: Copy Public IP Address
Open instance details and copy:
Public IPv4 Address
Example:
51.20.79.103
________________________________________
Step 10: Open Ubuntu Linux Terminal
Shortcut:
CTRL + ALT + T
________________________________________
Step 11: Go to Downloads Folder
Run:
cd ~/Downloads
________________________________________
Step 12: Check PEM File
Run:
ls
Output should contain:
firstkey.pem
________________________________________
Step 13: Give Permission to PEM File
Run:
chmod 400 firstkey.pem
This secures the key file.
________________________________________
Step 14: Connect to EC2 Instance
Run:
ssh -i firstkey.pem ubuntu@51.20.79.103
________________________________________
Step 15: Accept Connection
If asked:
Are you sure you want to continue connecting?
Type:
yes
________________________________________
Step 16: Successful Connection
You will see:
ubuntu@ip-172-31-xx-xx:~$
Now the local Ubuntu system is connected to the AWS Ubuntu server.
________________________________________
Step 17: Update Ubuntu Server
Run:
sudo apt update
________________________________________
Step 18: Install Python
Run:
sudo apt install python3 -y
________________________________________
Step 19: Create Python Program
Run:
nano hello.py
Type the following code:
print("Hello from AWS EC2")
________________________________________
Step 20: Save the File
Press:
CTRL + O
Press:
ENTER
Exit:
CTRL + X
________________________________________
Step 21: Run Python Program
Run:
python3 hello.py
Output:
Hello from AWS EC2
________________________________________
Step 22: Exit Server
Run:
exit


















